>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `[arith]`

``` hol4
Theorem theorem_name[arith]:
  statement
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Registers a persistent extra fact for linear arithmetic.

The argument-free `[arith]` theorem attribute adds its theorem verbatim to
the arithmetic fact set. Declarations are inherited through theory
ancestry and are read dynamically by the linarith tactics,
`LINARITH_ss`, and `linarith_solver`. The shipped set is initially empty.
Because facts are not automatically specialised, a universally quantified
declaration may be less useful than a fact about a named constant.

Use `linarithData.remove_arith` to remove a declaration persistently.
The `[arith]` set is independent of the operator rules in
`[arith_split]`.

### Failure

The attribute takes no arguments. A declared theorem may simply be
irrelevant to a particular arithmetic call.

### Example

``` hol4
Definition linarith_threshold_def:
  linarith_threshold = (7 : num)
End

Theorem linarith_threshold_lower_bound[arith]:
  3 <= linarith_threshold
Proof
  simp [linarith_threshold_def]
QED

Theorem arith_attribute_example:
  2 < linarith_threshold
Proof
  linarithLib.LINARITH_TAC []
QED
```

